<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Monthly Rental</span>
<h1>Expats: Maintenance Expectations in Hanoi | Hanoi Motorbike Guide</h1>
<p>A month of daily riding is a maintenance story, and the expat who rents long-term inherits a simple division of labour, the shop keeps the machine honest and the rider keeps the watching honest, and everything else is a conversation at the counter. What a rental month never asks of you is the ownership burden, no oil changes in your kitchen, no parts hunting on a Sunday, but it does ask the small daily attention that keeps a working machine working, and the expectations worth holding are the ones this page sets out plainly, without inventing the service guarantees, response times or policies that only the desk can state.</p>
<p>The machine and its support come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu at 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, and the month&rsquo;s maintenance conversation begins at handover. Start at the <a href="/monthly-motorbike-rental-hanoi/">monthly motorbike rental in Hanoi</a> hub, compare the numbers at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a> guide, see the fleet and terms at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, read the <a href="/monthly-motorbike-rental-hanoi/motorbike-rental-for-expats-hanoi/">motorbike rental for expats</a> guide for the long-stay picture, and browse the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for the daily habits that prevent most of what maintenance repairs.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">The handover sets the baseline</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">The rider&rsquo;s daily checks</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">The wear a month honestly shows</a></li>
